# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use TEM, a quantum function by Algorithmiq, to recover the dynamics of a 31-qubit kicked Ising chain from noisy hardware data, and compare it with PEC and ZNE."
msgstr "Gunakan TEM, fungsi kuantum oleh Algorithmiq, untuk memulihkan dinamik rantai Ising bertendang 31 qubit daripada data perkakasan berhingar, dan bandingkan dengan PEC dan ZNE."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate a kicked Ising model with the TEM function"
msgstr "Mensimulasikan model Ising ditendang dengan fungsi TEM"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"tutorials/simulate-kicked-ising-tem.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"tutorials/simulate-kicked-ising-tem.ipynb\" />\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore Floquet, linestyles, informationally */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore Floquet, linestyles, informationally */}\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithmiq's Tensor-network Error Mitigation (TEM) method is a hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that removes the effect of hardware noise entirely in classical post-processing. The circuit runs on the QPU as written, with an informationally complete (IC) measurement at the end. A tensor network that inverts the learned noise of the device is then applied to the measurement outcomes, giving error-mitigated expectation values.\n"
msgstr "Kaedah Tensor-network Error Mitigation (TEM) daripada Algorithmiq ialah algoritma hibrid kuantum-klasik yang menghapuskan sepenuhnya kesan hingar perkakasan dalam pasca-pemprosesan klasik. Litar dijalankan pada QPU seperti yang ditulis, dengan pengukuran informationally complete (IC) pada penghujungnya. Rangkaian tensor yang menyongsangkan hingar peranti yang dipelajari kemudian dikenakan pada hasil pengukuran, menghasilkan nilai jangkaan yang dikurangkan ralatnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial reproduces, at 31 qubits, the kind of many-body dynamics experiment run on up to 91 qubits in [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9). It shows:\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menghasilkan semula, pada 31 qubit, jenis eksperimen dinamik banyak jasad yang dijalankan sehingga 91 qubit dalam [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9). Ia menunjukkan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How much signal hardware noise destroys in a utility-scale dynamics circuit, and how much TEM recovers.\n"
msgstr "Sejauh mana isyarat dimusnahkan oleh hingar perkakasan dalam litar dinamik berskala utiliti, dan sejauh mana TEM memulihkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How TEM compares with probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) and zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) on the same circuit.\n"
msgstr "Bagaimana TEM dibandingkan dengan probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) dan zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) pada litar yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IC measurement also makes it possible to estimate observables that were not requested when the circuit ran, with a rerun of only the classical post-processing. For an example that estimates the full light cone of a chain, see [Run 4: measure the light cone from the same data](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning#run-4-measure-the-light-cone-from-the-same-data).\n"
msgstr "Pengukuran IC juga memungkinkan penganggaran observable yang tidak diminta semasa litar dijalankan, dengan hanya menjalankan semula pasca-pemprosesan klasik. Untuk contoh yang menganggar keseluruhan light cone bagi sesebuah rantai, lihat [Run 4: measure the light cone from the same data](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning#run-4-measure-the-light-cone-from-the-same-data).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To tune TEM's accuracy against its QPU and classical cost, see the companion example [Tune the TEM function for accuracy and cost](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning).\n"
msgstr "Untuk melaras ketepatan TEM berbanding kos QPU dan kos klasiknya, lihat contoh pelengkap [Tune the TEM function for accuracy and cost](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Usage estimate: approximately 20 QPU seconds for TEM on `ibm_phoenix` (the QPU time depends heavily on the chosen device). The optional PEC and ZNE comparison takes about 35 QPU minutes more, almost all of it for PEC.*\n"
msgstr "*Anggaran penggunaan: kira-kira 20 saat QPU untuk TEM pada `ibm_phoenix` (masa QPU sangat bergantung pada peranti yang dipilih). Perbandingan PEC dan ZNE pilihan mengambil kira-kira 35 minit QPU tambahan, hampir kesemuanya untuk PEC.*\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background: the kicked Ising chain {#background-the-kicked-ising-chain}"
msgstr "Latar belakang: rantai Ising bertendang {#background-the-kicked-ising-chain}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The kicked Ising model alternates an Ising evolution on a chain of $N$ qubits,\n"
msgstr "Model Ising bertendang berselang-seli antara evolusi Ising pada rantai $N$ qubit,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$ \\hat{H}_{\\text{I}} = J \\sum_{n=0}^{N-2} \\hat{Z}_n \\hat{Z}_{n+1} + h \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{Z}_n , $$\n"
msgstr "$$ \\hat{H}_{\\text{I}} = J \\sum_{n=0}^{N-2} \\hat{Z}_n \\hat{Z}_{n+1} + h \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{Z}_n , $$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with a transverse kick,\n"
msgstr "dengan tendangan melintang,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$ \\hat{H}_{K} = b \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{X}_n . $$\n"
msgstr "$$ \\hat{H}_{K} = b \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{X}_n . $$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One period of the dynamics is the Floquet unitary $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}} = e^{-i \\hat{H}_K} e^{-i \\hat{H}_I}$. On a quantum computer each period is a brickwork of two-qubit $ZZ$ rotations followed by single-qubit rotations, so the circuit contains only two distinct layers of two-qubit gates, repeated.\n"
msgstr "Satu tempoh dinamik ialah uniter Floquet $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}} = e^{-i \\hat{H}_K} e^{-i \\hat{H}_I}$. Pada komputer kuantum, setiap tempoh ialah susunan batu bata putaran $ZZ$ dua qubit diikuti putaran satu qubit, jadi litar hanya mengandungi dua lapisan get dua qubit yang berbeza, yang diulang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantity of interest is the infinite-temperature autocorrelation function of the first spin. The [reference paper](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) shows that it can be measured by preparing the first qubit in $|+\\rangle$ and every other pair of qubits in the Bell state $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$, evolving for $t$ periods, and measuring a single-qubit Pauli operator $\\hat{X}_n$.\n"
msgstr "Kuantiti yang diminati ialah fungsi autokorelasi suhu tak terhingga bagi spin pertama. [Kertas rujukan](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) menunjukkan bahawa ia boleh diukur dengan menyediakan qubit pertama dalam $|+\\rangle$ dan setiap pasangan qubit lain dalam keadaan Bell $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$, mengevolusi selama $t$ tempoh, dan mengukur operator Pauli satu qubit $\\hat{X}_n$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the dual unitary point $|J| = |b| = \\pi/4$ the model is exactly solvable:\n"
msgstr "Pada titik uniter dual $|J| = |b| = \\pi/4$, model ini boleh diselesaikan dengan tepat:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The correlation travels along the chain at maximal speed, so after $t$ periods only qubit $n = t$ carries it and $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n \\neq t} \\rangle = 0$.\n"
msgstr "Korelasi bergerak sepanjang rantai pada kelajuan maksimum, jadi selepas $t$ tempoh hanya qubit $n = t$ yang membawanya dan $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n \\neq t} \\rangle = 0$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "On that qubit, $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n=t} \\rangle = [\\cos(2h)]^t$.\n"
msgstr "Pada qubit itu, $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n=t} \\rangle = [\\cos(2h)]^t$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These exact values make the model a sharp benchmark for error mitigation: the signal that reaches qubit $t$ has passed through every layer of the circuit, so it is exposed to all the noise of the device, yet its noiseless value is known. Away from the dual unitary point the same circuits become hard to simulate classically, which is where the paper uses TEM to go beyond exact methods.\n"
msgstr "Nilai tepat ini menjadikan model ini penanda aras yang tajam bagi pengurangan ralat: isyarat yang sampai ke qubit $t$ telah melalui setiap lapisan litar, jadi ia terdedah kepada semua hingar peranti, namun nilai tanpa hingarnya diketahui. Jauh daripada titik uniter dual, litar yang sama menjadi sukar disimulasikan secara klasik, dan di situlah kertas tersebut menggunakan TEM untuk melangkaui kaedah tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEM works in three steps: it learns the noise of each distinct layer of two-qubit gates and the readout error, runs the circuit with an IC measurement, and finally applies the noise-inverting tensor network to the measurement outcomes on IBM Cloud&reg;.\n"
msgstr "TEM berfungsi dalam tiga langkah: ia mempelajari hingar bagi setiap lapisan get dua qubit yang berbeza serta ralat bacaan, menjalankan litar dengan pengukuran IC, dan akhirnya mengenakan rangkaian tensor penyongsang hingar pada hasil pengukuran di IBM Cloud&reg;.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Persediaan {#setup}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a prerequisite, ensure that the necessary dependencies are installed.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai prasyarat, pastikan kebergantungan yang diperlukan dipasang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Build the circuit and the observables {#step-1-build-the-circuit-and-the-observables}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Bina litar dan observable {#step-1-build-the-circuit-and-the-observables}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial uses a circuit that implements the kicked Ising model described in the previous section. The circuit is prepared as follows. First, there is a state preparation phase, in which the first qubit is in the state $|+\\rangle$, while the others are in Bell pairs $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$. This is followed by the brickwork structure that implements the unitary evolution $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}}$. The number of physical time steps corresponds to $t/2$ circuit layers.\n"
"The following code builds the circuit used in this tutorial.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tutorial ini menggunakan litar yang melaksanakan model Ising ditendang yang diterangkan dalam bahagian sebelumnya. Litar disediakan seperti berikut. Pertama, ada fasa penyediaan keadaan, di mana qubit pertama berada dalam keadaan $|+\\rangle$, manakala yang lain dalam pasangan Bell $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$. Ini diikuti oleh struktur bata yang melaksanakan evolusi unitari $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}}$. Bilangan langkah masa fizikal sepadan dengan $t/2$ lapisan litar.\n"
"Kod berikut membina litar yang digunakan dalam tutorial ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, build the observable, $\\hat{X}_{n=t}$. It is constructed as a simple Pauli string with the order matching the one used by Qiskit:\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, bina pemboleh ukur, $\\hat{X}_{n=t}$. Ia dibina sebagai rentetan Pauli mudah dengan susunan yang sepadan dengan yang digunakan oleh Qiskit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The experiment uses 31 qubits and 15 periods at $h = 0$, so the exact value of $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n=15} \\rangle$ is 1. This is a utility-scale circuit with 465 two-qubit gates: 15 that prepare the Bell pairs and 30 in each period. The signal that reaches qubit 15 passes through hundreds of them.\n"
msgstr "Eksperimen ini menggunakan 31 qubit dan 15 tempoh pada $h = 0$, jadi nilai tepat bagi $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n=15} \\rangle$ ialah 1. Ini ialah litar berskala utiliti dengan 465 get dua qubit: 15 yang menyediakan pasangan Bell dan 30 dalam setiap tempoh. Isyarat yang sampai ke qubit 15 melalui ratusan daripadanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Run TEM on the QPU {#step-2-run-tem-on-the-qpu}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Jalankan TEM pada QPU {#step-2-run-tem-on-the-qpu}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, get access to the TEM function and select a backend from the available devices. This code assumes you've already [saved your account](/guides/functions-get-started#install-qiskit-functions-catalog-client) to your local environment.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, dapatkan akses kepada fungsi TEM dan pilih Backend daripada peranti yang tersedia. Kod ini mengandaikan anda telah [menyimpan akaun anda](/guides/functions-get-started#install-qiskit-functions-catalog-client) ke persekitaran setempat anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the TEM function from the [IBM Quantum&reg; Functions Catalog](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/functions):\n"
msgstr "Muatkan fungsi TEM daripada [IBM Quantum&reg; Functions Catalog](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/functions):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile the circuit for the chosen device once, and map the observable onto the qubits it was placed on. TEM accepts this instruction set architecture (ISA) circuit as it is, and the PEC and ZNE comparison in Step 3 uses the same circuit, so all methods run the same gates on the same qubits.\n"
msgstr "Transpile litar untuk peranti yang dipilih sekali sahaja, dan petakan observable pada qubit tempat ia diletakkan. TEM menerima litar instruction set architecture (ISA) ini sebagaimana adanya, dan perbandingan PEC dan ZNE dalam Langkah 3 menggunakan litar yang sama, jadi semua kaedah menjalankan get yang sama pada qubit yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following options are based on the physics of the circuit:\n"
msgstr "Pilihan berikut berdasarkan fizik litar:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`max_layers_to_learn: 4`**: an upper bound on the number of distinct layers of two-qubit gates whose noise is learned. The brickwork has only two distinct layers, so only those two are learned.\n"
msgstr "**`max_layers_to_learn: 4`**: had atas bagi bilangan lapisan get dua qubit yang berbeza yang hingarnya dipelajari. Susunan batu bata hanya mempunyai dua lapisan yang berbeza, jadi hanya dua itu yang dipelajari.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`default_shots: 100_000`**: the number of shots of the IC measurement, which sets the statistical precision of the estimate.\n"
msgstr "**`default_shots: 100_000`**: bilangan shot pengukuran IC, yang menetapkan ketepatan statistik anggaran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`tem_max_bond_dimension: 128`** and **`tem_compression_cutoff: 1e-14`**: a moderate bond dimension that keeps the classical post-processing fast at 31 qubits, with a small cutoff so that the bond dimension is not truncated further.\n"
msgstr "**`tem_max_bond_dimension: 128`** dan **`tem_compression_cutoff: 1e-14`**: dimensi ikatan sederhana yang memastikan pasca-pemprosesan klasik kekal pantas pada 31 qubit, dengan potongan kecil supaya dimensi ikatan tidak dipangkas lagi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`private: False`**: keeps the job results downloadable later. Set it to `True` for confidential circuits.\n"
msgstr "**`private: False`**: memastikan keputusan kerja boleh dimuat turun kemudian. Tetapkan kepada `True` untuk circuit yang sulit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [performance tuning example](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning) explains each of these options in detail.\n"
msgstr "[Contoh penalaan prestasi](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning) menerangkan setiap pilihan ini secara terperinci.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the function size that the job needs with the size calculator provided by IBM&reg;, and pass it to `tem.run` as `function_size`. The calculator maps the circuit onto the backend and returns `S`, `M`, or `L` without submitting anything; see [Function sizes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/get-started#function-sizes).\n"
msgstr "Kirakan saiz fungsi yang diperlukan oleh kerja menggunakan kalkulator saiz yang disediakan oleh IBM&reg;, dan hantarkannya kepada `tem.run` sebagai `function_size`. Kalkulator memetakan circuit ke atas backend dan mengembalikan `S`, `M`, atau `L` tanpa menghantar apa-apa; lihat [Saiz fungsi](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/get-started#function-sizes).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, run the experiment, get the result, and visualize it. This step takes approximately 20 QPU seconds on `ibm_phoenix`.\n"
msgstr "Akhirnya, jalankan eksperimen, dapatkan keputusan, dan visualisasikan. Langkah ini mengambil masa kira-kira 20 saat QPU pada `ibm_phoenix`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Save the job ID. Use it to retrieve the results later with `catalog.get_job_by_id(job_id)`, or to rerun the post-processing.\n"
msgstr "Simpan ID kerja. Gunakannya untuk mendapatkan semula keputusan kemudian dengan `catalog.get_job_by_id(job_id)`, atau untuk menjalankan semula pasca-pemprosesan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Compare with PEC and ZNE {#step-3-compare-with-pec-and-zne}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Bandingkan dengan PEC dan ZNE {#step-3-compare-with-pec-and-zne}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The result metadata also contains the unmitigated estimate, computed from the same measurement outcomes without the noise-inverting network. A comparison of the two with the exact value shows how much of the signal the noise destroys, and how much TEM recovers:\n"
"To put the TEM result in context, run the same circuit with two other error mitigation methods: probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) and zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) with probabilistic error amplification (PEA).\n"
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The following code runs a large PEC experiment, which requires around 40 minutes of QPU time.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Metadata keputusan juga mengandungi anggaran tanpa mitigasi, yang dikira daripada hasil pengukuran yang sama tanpa rangkaian penyongsang hingar. Perbandingan kedua-duanya dengan nilai tepat menunjukkan berapa banyak isyarat yang dimusnahkan oleh hingar, dan berapa banyak yang dipulihkan oleh TEM:\n"
"Untuk meletakkan keputusan TEM dalam konteks, jalankan circuit yang sama dengan dua kaedah mitigasi ralat yang lain: pembatalan ralat kebarangkalian (PEC) dan ekstrapolasi sifar-hingar (ZNE) dengan pengamplifikasian ralat kebarangkalian (PEA).\n"
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Kod berikut menjalankan eksperimen PEC yang besar, yang memerlukan kira-kira 40 minit masa QPU.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Note:** Each mitigation method can produce expectation values that are either higher or lower than the exact result. The standard deviations reflect statistical uncertainty only; they do not account for inaccuracies in the characterized noise model, because that model has no associated error bound.\n"
msgstr "> **Nota:** Setiap kaedah mitigasi boleh menghasilkan nilai jangkaan yang lebih tinggi atau lebih rendah daripada keputusan tepat. Sisihan piawai hanya mencerminkan ketidakpastian statistik; ia tidak mengambil kira ketidaktepatan dalam model hingar yang dicirikan, kerana model itu tidak mempunyai batas ralat yang berkaitan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The unmitigated value decays with the number of noisy gates in the light cone of qubit 15, so at this depth most of the signal is lost. TEM removes this decay in post-processing, recovering most of the signal without running any additional circuits. The remaining gap to the exact value comes from the speed-oriented settings used in this tutorial: a bond dimension of 128 and a modest noise-learning budget. The [performance tuning example](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning) shows how to trade QPU and classical time for accuracy.\n"
msgstr "Nilai tanpa mitigasi merosot dengan bilangan gate berhingar dalam kon cahaya qubit 15, jadi pada kedalaman ini kebanyakan isyarat hilang. TEM menghapuskan kemerosotan ini dalam pasca-pemprosesan, memulihkan kebanyakan isyarat tanpa menjalankan sebarang circuit tambahan. Jurang yang tinggal berbanding nilai tepat datang daripada tetapan berorientasikan kelajuan yang digunakan dalam tutorial ini: dimensi ikatan 128 dan bajet pembelajaran hingar yang sederhana. [Contoh penalaan prestasi](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning) menunjukkan cara menukar masa QPU dan masa klasik untuk ketepatan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah seterusnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change $h$ in the circuit to move away from the exact value $[\\cos(2h)]^t = 1$, or away from the dual unitary point, where classical simulation becomes hard. See [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) for results up to 91 qubits.\n"
msgstr "Ubah $h$ dalam circuit untuk menjauhi nilai tepat $[\\cos(2h)]^t = 1$, atau menjauhi titik unitari dual, di mana simulasi klasik menjadi sukar. Lihat [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) untuk keputusan sehingga 91 qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
